<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 101.50 from 101.25, the Bundesbank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the Series 120 paper to 4.64 percent from 4.70 percent.</p>
<p>The yield on five-year bonds was last changed twice on Monday.</p>
<p>The 120 Series will expire in August 2001.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
